Subject: [clr] ppc64le: arch detection, kernarg read-back fences, spin hint

Portability fix worth sending upstream (ROCm/rocm-systems, projects/clr).

rocclr/include/top.hpp knows ARM and x86 and defines nothing for any other
host, which is mostly harmless (Os::spinPause() silently becomes a no-op),
except that device/rocm/rocvirtual.cpp and hipamd/src/hip_graph_internal.cpp
call _mm_sfence()/_mm_mfence() with no arch guard at all, around the
write-then-read-back that flushes the large-BAR kernarg buffer.  ppc64le
fails to compile there.

* top.hpp: ATI_ARCH_PPC64 for __powerpc64__, and under it the two fence
  names as a full `sync`.  The buffer they guard is device memory mapped
  caching-inhibited on POWER; Power ISA 3.0B Book II 4.6.1 excludes such
  storage from lwsync's ordering, so a release fence would compile and
  order nothing.
* os.cpp: Os::spinPause() lowers and restores SMT priority
  (`or 1,1,1; or 2,2,2`), the powerpc kernel's cpu_relax(), instead of
  falling through to nothing.

diff -ruN a/rocclr/include/top.hpp b/rocclr/include/top.hpp
--- a/rocclr/include/top.hpp	2026-05-19 16:18:44.000000000 -0600
+++ b/rocclr/include/top.hpp	2026-09-10 21:49:11.802360792 -0600
@@ -28,6 +28,18 @@
     defined(__x86__) || defined(__x86_64) || defined(__x86_64__) || defined(__amd64) ||            \
     defined(__amd64__) || defined(_M_X64) || defined(_M_AMD64)
 #define ATI_ARCH_X86
+#elif defined(__powerpc64__)
+#define ATI_ARCH_PPC64
+#endif
+
+#if defined(ATI_ARCH_PPC64)
+// rocvirtual.cpp and hip_graph_internal.cpp fence the large-BAR kernarg
+// read-back with the x86 spellings.  Those pages are caching-inhibited on
+// POWER, and only a full `sync` orders a cacheable store ahead of a subsequent
+// caching-inhibited one (Power ISA 3.0B Book II 4.6.1; lwsync excludes CI
+// storage), so both fences are the full barrier here.
+static inline void _mm_sfence(void) { __asm__ __volatile__("sync" ::: "memory"); }
+static inline void _mm_mfence(void) { __asm__ __volatile__("sync" ::: "memory"); }
 #endif
 
 #if defined(ATI_ARCH_ARM)
diff -ruN a/rocclr/os/os.cpp b/rocclr/os/os.cpp
--- a/rocclr/os/os.cpp	2026-05-19 16:18:44.000000000 -0600
+++ b/rocclr/os/os.cpp	2026-09-10 21:49:11.802704852 -0600
@@ -125,6 +125,9 @@
   _mm_pause();
 #elif defined(ATI_ARCH_ARM)
   __asm__ __volatile__("yield");
+#elif defined(ATI_ARCH_PPC64)
+  // Lower then restore SMT thread priority; the powerpc kernel's cpu_relax().
+  __asm__ __volatile__("or 1,1,1\n\tor 2,2,2" ::: "memory");
 #endif
 }
 
